From b9af2260cee4e3f1a1cebe53a6107d3a8780d873 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adpena <adpena@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 06:43:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] WIP (unverified): runtime work toward the Linux-only test
 aborts (HF-06)

Preserved from the cifix-rtabort lane (gpt-6.1-sol), which stopped mid-task
without a report. NOT landed on main; verify on Linux before merging.

Contents: a restructuring of builtins/concurrent.rs future error handling,
runtime_state shutdown and functools changes aimed at keeping panics and
resume_unwind from crossing extern "C" boundaries, test_module_gil_declarations
fixes, and related test adjustments.

State on Windows at preservation: cargo fmt and clippy (molt-runtime,
molt-lang-cpython-abi, all targets) clean; test_module_gil_declarations
7 passed. builtins::concurrent::tests::future_errors_use_supplied_classes_...
and builtins::module_table::tests::builtin_bootstrap_publication_... still
fail here, as they do on main. The full molt-runtime lib suite deadlocks
after ~71 tests on Windows on main too, so no full-suite comparison exists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
